# Sprint E3.2 connection-detail redaction gap closure (Lead review item, sanitized)
# run_id: 20261110-1647 (UTC)
# Scope: src/lib/observability/redact.ts only. Event names/fields and the log schema are
# unchanged; this tightens what the existing redactor treats as sensitive.

## Added rules
# - whole-value replacement (err.message / field values) when text carries:
#     "Can't reach database server at ..."       (Prisma P1001 wording)
#     "connection to server at ..., port N failed" (node-postgres wording)
#     "ECONNREFUSED ..."
#     localhost:<port> or IPv4:<port>
# - in-place scrubbing of the same patterns inside stacks, so remaining frames stay usable
# - ordinary source references such as RequestHandler.ts:237:13 or src/lib/db.ts:12:3 are
#   explicitly NOT treated as host:port (unit test).

## Unit evidence (npm run test:unit, exit=0; 125 tests / 12 files)
# src/lib/observability/redact.vitest.ts (17 tests) includes:
#   "replaces Prisma/node-postgres host:port messages as a whole"
#   "scrubs host:port and Prisma wording from stacks while keeping source frames"
#   "does not confuse ordinary source line references with host:port details"
# src/lib/observability/logger.vitest.ts (15 tests) includes:
#   "never serializes database host:port connection details"
#     asserts the serialized record contains no "localhost:5432" and no ":5432",
#     err.message == [redacted], err.code == P1001, err.name preserved
# run command: npx vitest run src/lib/observability
#   Test Files 5 passed (5) / Tests 53 passed (53) exit=0

